#changes in the config.sys file and autoexec file- yes I rebooted),
#the .exe file spits out term nansi-color not found.
#Has anybody got it to work who redefined the path for the these
#files. Also, has anyone got it to work with ansi.sys. I failed at
#that to, but I had to go, and couldn't fuddle with it to much.

Set the environment variable TERMCAP=/<directory#[/subdirectory][/...]/termcap
(e.g. if your termcap file is in c:\foo\bar then set
TERMCAP=/foo/bar/termcap.)  Then set TERM=nansi-color OR nansi-mono OR
ansi-color OR ansi-mono.  The .cnf file is not used for this.  Put these
definitions in your autoexec.bat file, or enter them just before executing the
'nethack' command.

